  <div id="sutta">
  
            <h4 id="thag4.10" class="h1">Thag 4:10  Dhammika</h4>
            <div class="verse">
              <p>The Dhamma protects</p>
              <p>those who live by the Dhamma.</p>
              <p>The Dhamma well-practiced</p>
              <p class="v1">brings bliss.</p>
              <p>This—the reward</p>
              <p>when the Dhamma’s well-practiced:</p>
              <p>One who lives by the Dhamma</p>
              <p>doesn’t go to a bad destination.</p>
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p>For Dhamma and non-</p>
                <p>don’t bear equal results.</p>
                <p>Non-Dhamma leads you to hell;</p>
                <p>Dhamma, to a good destination.</p>
                <p>So you should engender desire</p>
                <p>for acts of Dhamma,</p>
                <p class="v2">rejoicing</p>
                <p>in the One     Well-Gone,</p>
                <p>the one      who is Such.</p>
                <p>Standing firm in the Dhamma,</p>
                <p>of the foremost</p>
                <p>One Well-Gone,</p>
                <p>his disciples are guided</p>
                <p>—enlightened—</p>
                <p>to the foremost</p>
                <p>refuge supreme.</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
              <div class="verse-add">
                <p>Burst       is the root of the boil;</p>
                <p>the net of craving     uprooted.</p>
                <p>He, having ended his wandering-on,</p>
                <p>has no stain—</p>
                <p>like the moon</p>
                <p>on a clear full-moon night.</p>
              </div><!--end verse-add-->
            </div><!--end verse-->
      </div><!--end:sutta-->
    </div><!--end:content-->
    
